  "text_sanskrit": "न वेदयज्ञाध्ययनैर्न दानैर्- न च क्रियाभिर्न तपोभिरुग्रैः । एवंरूपः शक्य अहं नृलोके द्रष्टुं त्वदन्येन कुरुप्रवीर ॥ ११-४८ ॥",
  "itrans": "na vedayaj~nAdhyayanairna dAnair- na cha kriyAbhirna tapobhirugraiH . eva.nrUpaH shakya ahaM nR^iloke draShTuM tvadanyena kurupravIra .. 11-48 ..",
  "translation": "Neither by the study of Vedas and sacrifices, nor by charitable gifts, nor by righteous works, nor by severe austerities, I of such form, am possible to be seen by any other than thyself, O warrior of Kuru race. (48) \nV. By any other, 8c., i.e., by any inferior in the scale of eligibility, in the same degree as it was possible for Arjun. If not thus interpreted this passage would be contradictory to the several statements already made. (48)",
